Instead of interruptions fragmenting your day, you can trust that everything gets done at the best time.';
    END IF;
    SELECT id INTO v_note_id FROM public.note
        WHERE thread_id = v_thread_id AND key = 'focuses' AND link_id IS NULL AND archived_at IS NULL LIMIT 1;
    IF v_note_id IS NULL THEN
        INSERT INTO public.note (author_id, created_by, thread_id, source_created_at, content, key)
            VALUES (c_system_instance_id, c_system_instance_id, v_thread_id, now() + (1 * interval '1 minute'), 'By bringing all you work together, Plot eliminates time and attention lost to jump around tools. Instead of organizing your work by _where_ it is, you organize it by _how_ you work on it. This lets you make real progress in an area you choose.

Create focuses for:

- _Important projects_: With everything related to a project in one focus, you can find what you need quickly, with a clear view of what''s outstanding. Even better, you can send related messages and replies without getting pulled into unrelated work that happens to be in the same chat, inbox, or app.
- _Core roles_: At work, you might have direct responsibilities while also managing others. Putting these in separate focuses ensures you make progress on your goals while giving your team the attention they deserve.
- _Secondary roles_: Your work for extra roles you take on, like volunteering, can easily slip. Create a focus and schedule it once a week to deliver on your commitments.
- _Key activities_: Certain activities are done best with concentrated focus, like customer and sales conversations, or reviewing progress from a large team. In a focus, you choose how much and how often to invest your time.

Focuses aren''t just for the high priority stuff. By creating focuses for low-urgency items, you can safely ignore them for days before efficiently catching up. Reading, promotions, and unsolicited requests often fit here.', 'focuses');
    ELSE
